  "notes": "Source species are visual/ecological analogues for Asterra, not literal Earth taxonomy. Surface textures are intentionally deferred to a later terrain-material milestone.",
  "biome_plan": {
    "OCEAN": "No generic v1 mesh scatter. Keep deep ocean visually clean until a verified CC0 benthic/kelp/coral set is sourced; bathymetric rock comes from terrain/geology.",
    "SHELF_SEA": "Sparse coastal stones, ledges and pebble patches in shallow rocky areas. Dedicated kelp/seagrass remains an explicit asset gap.",
    "ICE_CAP": "Extremely sparse exposed stone and boulder scatter only where ice/snow cover permits.",
    "TUNDRA": "Low moss, short/dry grass, low weeds, small shrubs, stones and occasional boulders; no tall canopy.",
    "TAIGA": "Fir/pine canopy, saplings, moss, fern, low shrubs, mossy rocks, roots, stumps and fallen logs.",
    "COLD_DESERT": "Sparse dry grass, quartz/stone scatter, weathered boulders and dead plant debris.",
    "TEMPERATE_GRASSLAND": "Dense mixed grasses with weeds/wildflowers, sparse shrubs, stones and rare boulders.",
    "TEMPERATE_FOREST": "Broadleaf canopy, shrubs, fern/moss ground cover, roots, stumps, fallen logs and mossy rocks.",
    "TEMPERATE_RAINFOREST": "Very dense moss/fern/shrub layer, broadleaf/coastal-form trees, deadwood, exposed roots and moss-covered rocks.",
    "MEDITERRANEAN": "Dry grass, dense scrub, low wind-shaped trees, dry branches, stones and warm weathered boulders.",
    "STEPPE": "Patchy dry grasses, low shrubs, weeds, stones and occasional boulders/dead debris.",
    "HOT_DESERT": "Succulents and desert shrubs at low density, dry leaves/branches, quartz stones and weathered desert boulders.",
    "SAVANNA": "Bermuda/dry grasses, scattered shrubs, sparse broadleaf trees, deadwood and exposed rocks.",
    "TROPICAL_SEASONAL_FOREST": "Broadleaf trees with tropical shrubs/groundcover, seasonal grass openings, deadwood and roots.",
    "TROPICAL_RAINFOREST": "Dense broadleaf canopy, tropical understory, fern, moss, shrubs, roots, deadwood and mossy rocks.",
    "WETLAND": "Wet grasses, fern, nettle/weed groundcover, shrubs and sparse moisture-tolerant trees. Reeds/cattails are an explicit v1 asset gap.",
    "ALPINE": "Sparse low grass/moss in sheltered areas with dominant stones, scree and boulders; no trees above the ecological treeline.",
    "BARE_ROCK": "Geology-driven stones, boulders and ledges only; vegetation limited to rare crevice moss/grass when climate allows."
  },
